/**
  @page examples-mmg-index Working with MMG
  @brief Choose a mesh-processing workflow and understand its guarantees.

  MMG operations produce a new mesh topology. Optimization improves element
  shape, while adaptation uses a prescribed size field. The examples separate
  these tasks from mesh conversion and metadata handling.

  - @subpage examples-mmg-simple_io — Read and write MMG mesh data.
  - @subpage examples-mmg-casting — Work with MMG and Geometry mesh interfaces.
  - @subpage examples-mmg-mesh_optimization — Improve element quality.
  - @subpage examples-mmg-mesh_adaptation — Adapt to a field or metric.
  - @subpage examples-mmg-behavior — Required entities, level-set cuts, and
    preservation guarantees.

  Read the behavior guide before relying on entity indices or feature metadata
  across a remeshing operation.

  @m_footernavigation
*/
